+# Agent Note: Raw stream activity refreshes the provider idle deadline
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-17-raw-stream-activity-refreshes-idle-deadline.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The pi-ai adapter refreshed its idle watchdog only when pi-ai emitted a parsed assistant event. OpenAI-compatible SSE comments are transport activity but produce no assistant event, so an upstream that remained alive through heartbeat comments could be aborted as idle. Extending the timeout delayed the same false positive without distinguishing a live generation from a hung connection.
+
+The same path trusted a provider's terminal `tool_calls` finish reason even when output usage reached the requested token cap. A truncated argument stream can sometimes be repaired into valid JSON with required fields missing; treating that terminal reason as executable could send an incomplete write request to the local tool layer.
+
+## Decision
+
+The OpenAI Chat Completions implementation in the pinned pi-ai dependency exposes an `onActivity` callback and invokes it for every response-body chunk before SSE parsing. `PiAiAdapter` connects that callback to its existing idle watchdog. The callback carries no bytes and creates no stream chunk, so comments and heartbeat frames refresh liveness without entering assistant content, replay state, or the session log.
+
+The dependency change is a package-manager patch rather than a second HTTP client in the adapter. It preserves pi-ai's provider parsing and cancellation while adding the missing transport observation point. The patch is limited to OpenAI Chat Completions, which is the deployed gateway protocol that needs comment heartbeat support.
+
+Tool execution retains its terminal commit point. When pi-ai reports `toolUse` and cumulative output usage is at or above the exact output cap sent for the request, the adapter maps the response to `max-tokens`; the agent loop therefore does not execute the tool block. Tool calls below the cap keep the existing `tool-calls` result and still pass through ordinary schema validation before execution.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Increasing `streamIdleTimeoutMs`.** This accommodates one observed pause but preserves the category error: a responsive heartbeat-only stream and a silent broken stream remain indistinguishable until a larger timer expires.
+- **Generating synthetic heartbeats in AI Relay.** This would keep DSH alive even when the model server itself had stopped producing activity, masking the failure the idle watchdog is intended to detect. Relay forwards upstream activity instead.
+- **Refreshing only on parsed pi-ai events.** Tool argument deltas already follow this path, but SSE comments intentionally do not. Keeping the parsed-event boundary cannot represent transport liveness without turning comments into fake model content.
+- **Executing repaired tool JSON and relying only on schema validation.** Validation catches a missing required field, but classifying a response known to end at its output cap as complete gives every tool schema an avoidable malformed call and can still admit semantically truncated optional content.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Heartbeat comments can safely cover long model-side pauses while the upstream connection remains active, and genuine upstream silence still reaches the existing timeout. The harness stores no heartbeat record and model-visible history is unchanged.
+
+The repository carries a narrow pi-ai patch until upstream provides a raw activity callback. A pi-ai upgrade must re-evaluate or retire that patch. Output-cap detection depends on usage returned by the provider; providers that omit or misreport usage still rely on their finish reason and normal tool schema validation.
+
+## Testing
+
+The adapter test server emits heartbeat-only SSE comments for longer than the configured idle interval before resuming model output. The request completes, and the assembled assistant message contains only the model text. Stream conversion tests also pin that a tool finish at the requested cap becomes `max-tokens`, while the same tool finish below the cap remains `tool-calls`.
